WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on
your Grammy nomination.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, you've been
nominated for Grammys before.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:06.039
This is the first time that
it has not been a collaboration.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. I was nominated with
Pink.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.509 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I was nominated with

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mac McAnally, Grace Potter,
and some other people.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:15.582
But this is the first time that
I've been nominated for

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.750 line:92%
something solely that I created.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's very exciting.
Congratulations.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was the
difference this time?

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've obviously had a lot of
solo work over the years.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think we just did
a lot of things that was

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:28.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
left of center than how
we usually release a record.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had a single.
Then we changed it.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.232 size:78% position:39%
I had an album title,
and we changed it.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Cosmic Hallelujah"
wasn't even the album title.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.404 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-What was it before?

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.138 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I can't even remember.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that means
you made the right choice.

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we did a lot of
interesting things.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:46.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
I made a video for a song
that we knew that

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
wasn't gonna be a single,
called "Rich and Miserable."

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:49.549 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-"Rich and Miserable."

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:53.186
-And my friend John McGinley,
who's a wonderful actor --

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wonderful actor.
"Scrubs" and "Platoon."

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He played
this college professor

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
at Columbia University
here in New York.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.662 line:92%
and just did a brilliant job.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was --
You know, sometimes,

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.667
record labels don't like it when
you go and make a video

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.570
on a song that's really
expensive, when they know

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's not gonna be
a single on the radio.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.374 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But we did it anyway.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that
it was things like that

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:21.214 size:81% position:41%
that really allowed us
to dig a little deeper

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.715 line:92%
than you normally do on a record

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:27.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you just traditionally
release the singles

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.155 line:92%
and do the marketing plan.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.857 line:92%
It was chaos from the beginning.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:34.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I felt like that, somehow,
it's worked out in the end.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.228 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, that's fantastic.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
You mentioned that
you shot this at college.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.565 line:92%
Your first song -- Is it true

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
you wrote your
first song in college?

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:41.367 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And what led you
to write your first song?

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:47.607
-I was in -- Ironically enough,
I was in a persuasion class.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.478
-Okay. I feel like they
don't have those anymore.

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:54.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there was
a girl sitting next to me

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:59.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I was trying to persuade
to go out with me.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.253 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, wow.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:04.290
-And so I thought that
I would write her a song.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Very persuasive.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:10.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so I stayed up
in my apartment off campus

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I tried to write
this girl a song.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was -- Some of you
may know what a cassette is.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
You probably still remember
what a cassette is.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.271 line:92%
I put it down on a cassette.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.205 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You know, you had to hit

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
the play and record
at the same time?

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, so, I did that
with my guitar

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I took it
to class the next day.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she sat
right beside me in class.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.215 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I slid it to her.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:32.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
Didn't say anything,
didn't even look at her.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.654 line:92%
All right? I just went...

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:39.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know, class ends.
I go home.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.761 line:92%
I come back the next day.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.962 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And she was, like --

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.532
Remember, she was sitting
right here at this table.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I walked into
class the next day,

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:52.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she was sitting in
the far corner of the class.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, that --

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.742 size:88% position:44%
-That's amazing that you
persuaded her to move.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:58.244
-Well, it was my -- Yeah, I did.
-Yeah.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it was literally
my first taste of

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.551 line:92%
rejection in the music business.

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, that's good.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
It certainly
turned around for you.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now I want to talk
about the fans.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:11.858
Kenny Chesney fans refer to
themselves as "No Shoes Nation."

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you have fans
that travel for your shows.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
You obviously want them to
have a good experience.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:18.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it true that when you --
'Cause you play big --

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:21.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play arenas.
You play football stadiums.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
That you go sit in
the worst seat

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
before the show starts just
so you have a sense of

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.406 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
exactly the gap?

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. We get there
on a Friday,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if we're playing
a Saturday stadium show,

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
we get there and do
sound check on Friday night.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I will go --
Just because I want to

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:40.920 size:81% position:41%
emotionally, visually,
and mentally measure

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
how far I have to go
when I'm onstage

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:47.060
to reach the people in the very
top of that football stadium.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:47.727 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And unless I go up there

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:51.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sit and absorb it all,
I don't really know.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:55.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, I know what it looks like
from the stage up there,

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I have to visually see
what it looks like

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.106 size:88% position:44% line:92%
from up there down here.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:00.907 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And that's why I do it.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's one of
the things that I do,

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.911 line:92%
because I tell you, Seth --

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
the connection we have
out there onstage

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:11.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the most unbelievable thing
I've ever felt in my life.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:11.985 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And we have people --

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like you said,
we have people that travel.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have people that
really care about the music.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:18.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, we've been
doing this for a little while.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:24.030
And that relationship with them
has been built so strongly

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the years,
and I'm very proud of them.

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:28.368
And it's one of the reasons that
we're able to do what we do.

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's fantastic
that you do that.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.738 line:92%
I want to talk about another --

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:34.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
a place you have
a connection with,

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.341 line:92%
which is the Virgin Islands.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had a house in St. John's.
-I did.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And after the hurricane,
you were one of

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:43.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first planes
to go down there to help out.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
You started a charitable
organization.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you tell us
a little bit about it?

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I started a foundation called
Love for Love City.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Love City is
the nickname of St. John.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that place,
the Virgin Islands,

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.662 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the BVIs and U.S. V.I.,

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:58.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
has been a place
that has really fed me,

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
as an individual,
over the years.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.968 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It's fed me as a human.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been a huge part
of my adult life

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it has been a really big
source of creativeness.

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:13.846 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It's fed me creatively.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's fed me
emotionally and mentally.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's been a healer.

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:20.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been
so many things in my life.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.121 line:92%
And when that happened, to --

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wasn't there the night
the storm happened,

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I was home
and I was watching it,

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:26.926 line:92%
like the rest of the world.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:30.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to see that storm cell go
right over the island,

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I could know
where my house is.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:37.403
And I had 17 people inside my
house, going through the storm.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:41.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was the most anxiety
I'd ever felt in my life.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:42.275 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It really was.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:45.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I knew then that
I was going to do something

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:47.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
to help the island,
to help the people.

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we started
Love for Love City,

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:53.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's been an unbelievable
thing to be a part of.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was you
heading down there, right?

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-There you go.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, so, I had an
island dog named Cookie.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:05:59.926 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:03.529
And Cookie -- We had to bring
Cookie back after the storm.

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:06.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've got
this assistant named Jill.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:06.799 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And Jill loves dogs.

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:10.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Cookie died in Jill's arms
at my house in Tennessee.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:14.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
It had only been off
the island never, until then.

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's why you see
what you see there.

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:19.979
That's when I decided that
we were not only going to try to

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.447 line:92%
help the people on the island,

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were gonna help
the dogs and the animals,

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:27.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they were
as displaced as anyone else.

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:30.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's fantastic.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's really great
that you did that.

